ac:Schema 7 and every new wire artifact are closed, versioned and implementation-ready; external source is resolved, raw-snapshot validated, hashed and independently audited before cache or compiler work; inaccessible sources follow typed offline-warning versus install/audit hard-failure semantics; package-controlled argv, environment, output paths, executable names, credentials, hooks, signing and generic language drivers remain forbidden. Schemas 1-5 remain byte compatible and schema-6/7 declaration shapes stay closed. go-v1 normatively identifies a portable manager-worker-v1 execution policy with honest capability evidence and no hardened claim; portable versus future hardened cache, receipt, marker and claim identities cannot alias. Generated cases, validators, compatibility guards, deterministic regeneration and rc.5 release gates pass.
